    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A poet of the night, Alfred Benezri was Embraced in Damascus in the 1760s by the enigmatic Moraye, and fled the Syrian night for Montreal after his sire's destruction, where Saint Ignace accepted him as a student despite his \"alien\" Sunni Muslim heritage. A political pragmatist, Alfred proposed the coven's rotating leadership after Ignace's Sainting and helped design the modern @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} Inquisition alongside Black Hand Dominion Julian, later serving as a judge inquisitor (1964&ndash;1981) and knight inquisitor (until 1993). He tortures mortals to record their dying utterances as inspiration for his poetry, and now stands as the Shepherds' candidate to replace foreign Archbishop Carolina Valez and restore the city's traditional, scholarly Sabbat order.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Haunted by responsibility; you present a strong, competent front to hide a melancholic heart. You are visibly uncomfortable with the political backing of the Queens of Mercy given your traditional views on gender.</p><h2>Secrets</h2><p>Alfred is deeply suspicious of &quot;DeSoto,&quot; whose sudden retreat into seclusion after Sangris' trial struck him as deeply out of character for a dedicated inquisitor.</p>",
    "notes": "Embraced 1769. Apparent age: late 40s. Path of Nocturnal Redemption 7. Disciplines (as printed): Auspex 4, Dominate 3, Fortitude 2, Presence 4, Thaumaturgy 4 (Gift of Morpheus 4, Spirit Thaumaturgy 3).",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
